sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client as Customer / API Client
    participant API as TicketController
    participant Idem as IdempotencyFilter
    participant DB as PostgreSQL 16 (ticket_db)
    participant Poller as OutboxPoller (1s Fixed Delay)
    participant Kafka as Apache Kafka (KRaft)
    participant Consumer as AI Event Consumer

    Client->>Idem: POST /api/v1/tickets (Idempotency-Key: abc-123)
    Idem->>DB: Check idempotency_records WHERE key = 'abc-123'
    alt Key already exists (Replay)
        DB-->>Idem: Cached Response (201 Created)
        Idem-->>Client: Return cached 201 + (X-Idempotent-Replay: true)
    else Key is new
        Idem->>API: Execute Ticket Creation
        API->>DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION
        API->>DB: INSERT INTO tickets (...) VALUES (...)
        API->>DB: INSERT INTO outbox_events (event_type='ticket.created.v1', status='PENDING', payload=...)
        API->>DB: INSERT INTO idempotency_records (key='abc-123', status_code=201, payload=...)
        API->>DB: COMMIT TRANSACTION
        Note over DB: Single atomic commit prevents dual-write failures!
        API-->>Client: HTTP 201 Created

        loop Every 1 Second
            Poller->>DB: SELECT * FROM outbox_events WHERE status = 'PENDING' FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
            Poller->>Kafka: Produce record to 'ticket.events.v1' (Key = tenantId)
            Kafka-->>Poller: ACK RecordMetadata(offset=102)
            Poller->>DB: UPDATE outbox_events SET status = 'PUBLISHED', published_at = NOW()
        end

        Kafka->>Consumer: Deliver ticket.created.v1
        Note over Consumer: Inbox check deduplicates by eventId
    end
